# KNOWN GAP repro — the self-host move checker's fall-through classifier
# `match_has_catch_all` (`tests/fixtures/self_host_typechecker/typecheck.gg`)
# credits an UNGUARDED `PBinding` as a catch-all WITHOUT consulting the enum's
# variant list. `case Value:` parses as a `PBinding`, not a `PConstructor`, and
# whether a bare name is an irrefutable catch-all or names a VARIANT cannot be
# decided without `all_variants` in hand — the exact ambiguity the ported
# exhaustiveness check goes to lengths to avoid by deciding `PBinding` inside
# `collect_covered_variants` instead of in the pre-resolution scan.
#
# CELL: pattern shape = BARE UNQUALIFIED VARIANT NAME x consumer = the move
# checker's fall-through question (all three `match_has_catch_all` consumers:
# the `SMatch` join, the `EMatch` join, the `live_stmt_diverges` divergence
# gate). The exhaustiveness half of this same pattern shape is sampled by
# `tests/fixtures/exhaustiveness/neg_bare_variant.gg` (refutable) and
# `pos_binding_catchall.gg` (irrefutable); the LIVENESS half — this cell — had
# no sample, and is named as unsampled in the doc comment of the `tests/lints.rs`
# guard `self_host_match_fallthrough_predicates_pinned`.
#
# INTENDED: this program is REJECTED on BOTH lanes. Rust `gg check` already
# rejects it TWICE — `E_NonExhaustiveMatch` (missing `Next`, `Halt`) and
# `E_UseAfterMove` at `print(s)`. The self-host ACCEPTS it and lowers C.
#
# TWO MECHANISMS COMPOSE, and either fix alone flips this fixture to a reject:
#   1. the filed `infer_expr_type`/`RTRef` hole (see
#      `known_gaps/sh_field_off_method_call_untyped.gg`) leaves the scrutinee
#      `nodes.get(i).unwrap().kind` UNTYPED, so the newly-ported exhaustiveness
#      check conservatively bails and never emits `E_NonExhaustiveMatch`;
#   2. `match_has_catch_all` then tells the move checker there is no
#      fall-through, so the moved `s` is treated as re-initialised on every
#      path and `E_UseAfterMove` is never emitted either.
# Landing (1) makes this reject with `E_NonExhaustiveMatch`; landing (2) makes
# it reject with `E_UseAfterMove`. The `#[ignore]`d test accepts either, because
# either is the intended REJECT — what must never happen is the accept.
#
# ⚠ THE OBVIOUS FIX IS WRONG, AND WAS MEASURED WRONG. Deleting the
# `case PBinding(_): return true` arm makes THIS program reject — and makes the
# self-host OVER-REJECT a genuine irrefutable catch-all. Measured, on rebuilt
# drivers, rc read off the binary with stderr to a file:
#
#   probe                                     pristine        PBinding arm deleted
#   this fixture                              rc 0, 9248 B    rc 1, 0 B, E_UseAfterMove
#   the same shape with `case other:`         rc 0, 3616 B    rc 1, 0 B, E_UseAfterMove
#   (a NON-variant binding, i.e. a real catch-all — must stay ACCEPTED)
#
# So the fix has to be VARIANT-AWARE, which needs the enum's variant list
# threaded into a predicate whose ARMS-ONLY signature the lint deliberately
# pins (that widening is the fusion route the guard exists to block). That
# interaction is a DESIGN question — see the `TODO.md` bullet beginning
# "`match_has_catch_all` credits an unguarded `PBinding` as a catch-all".
#
# REGENERATE (never trust the bytes above — Core #5):
#   ./target/debug/gg check tests/fixtures/known_gaps/sh_variant_binding_credited_as_catchall.gg
#   ./target/debug/gg build tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver.gg
#   ./tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver \
#       tests/fixtures/known_gaps/sh_variant_binding_credited_as_catchall.gg \
#       lib --lir-c > /tmp/out.c 2> /tmp/out.err ; echo $?; wc -c /tmp/out.c
#
# The seed String is HEAP-FORCED (`mk()` concatenates) rather than a literal, so
# the moved-from read is a real allocation if the self-host ever starts dropping
# the `^`-moved parameter. Measured today the emitted binary prints the
# moved-from contents and is ASan-clean; the defect is the ACCEPT, not a
# currently-observable runtime trap.
enum Kind:
    Value()
    Next()
    Halt()

struct Node:
    Kind kind
    int payload

String mk():
    return "gg" + "-payload"

void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(Vector[Node] nodes, int i):
    String s = mk()
    sink(^s)
    match nodes.get(i).unwrap().kind:
        case Value:
            s = "reinit"
    print(s)

void main():
    Vector[Node] a = [Node(Kind.Halt(), 1)]
    probe(a, 0)
